03_p0127"><label>47.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Choo</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ireland</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sherriff</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An in vitro investigation into the use of resin-modified glass poly(alkenoate) cements as orthodontic bonding agents</article-title><source>Eur J Orthod</source><year>2001</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>243</fpage><lpage>252</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11471267</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="f1-dent03_p0127" position="float"><label>Figure 1.</label><caption><p>A set of laser fluorescence device (DIAGNOdent Pen, Kavo, Germany).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="p130_fig1"/></fig><fig id="f2-dent03_p0127" position="float"><label>Figure 2.</label><caption><p>Measurement of the demineralization on gingival side of the bracket by DIAGNOdent Pen.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="p130_fig2"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-dent03_p0127" position="float"><label>Table 1.</label><caption><p>Intra- and inter- examiner agreement in measurement of DIAGNOdent Pen values quantified by Cohen&#x02019;s Kappa.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Observation Type</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Kappa Score (K)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Intra-examiner agreement (examiner 1)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.89</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Intra-examiner agreement (examiner 2)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.85</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Inter-observer agreement</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.79</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn1-dent03_p0127"><p>K&#x0003c;0.40 poor agreement, K=0.41&#x02212;0.60 moderate agreement, K=0.61&#x02212;0.80 substantial agreement, K&#x0003c;0.75 almost perfect agreement.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t2-dent03_p0127" position="float"><label>Table 2.</label><caption><p>Descriptive statistics and the comparisons of three investigated bonding materials for demineralization variations (&#x00394;D) adjacent to orthodontic brackets.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="1">Testing Groups</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">N</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">&#x00394;D</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">SD</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">SE</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">Min</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">Max</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">F-value</th><th align="center" rowspan="2" colspan="1">P-value</th><th align="center" colspan="2" rowspan="1">Multiple Comparisons</th></tr><tr><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ACP-containing composite</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Resin Modified Glass Ionomer Cement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Orthodontic Composite (Control)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12.15</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.83</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.86</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6.75</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">17.50</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.005**</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.010*</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ACP-containing Orthodontic Composite</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">8.98</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.38</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.53</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5.00</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12.50</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6.650</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.003**</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">NS 0.964</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Resin Modified Glass Ionomer Cement</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">9.24</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.73</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.61</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6.25</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">17.00</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn2-dent03_p0127"><p>N indicates sample size; &#x00394;D: demineralization variation; SD: Standard deviation; SE: Standard error; ACP: amorphus calcium phosphate; RMGIC: resin modifed glass ionomer cement.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>